==========================================================================
D. NORM DICHOTOMY -- metallic (norm -1) vs reciprocal (norm +1)
==========================================================================
  x^2 - n x - 1 has root product -1, so the pair is {lam, -1/lam}: closed
  under r -> -1/r, an ANTI-reciprocal map, and containing a negative element.
  THM-3003 section 1's rigidity needs {r} = {mu/r} with mu = e_d^(2/d) > 0,
  i.e. norm +1 and positive roots.  So the two extremal strata cannot meet.

  test: are the metallic h-sequences antipalindromic (R_k = R_(d-k))?
    n=1 d=6: R = ['1', '1/2', '4/3', '9/10', '25/24']   antipalindromic? False
    n=2 d=6: R = ['1/2', '4/5', '25/24', '144/145', '841/840']   antipalindromic? False
    n=3 d=6: R = ['1/3', '9/10', '100/99', '1089/1090', '11881/11880']   antipalindromic? False
    antipalindromic in 0 of 9 cases (n=1,2,3 x d=6,7,8): True
  => maximal alternation (norm -1) and swap-stability (norm +1) are
     DISJOINT, not nested.  A two-element direction multiset cannot be in
     both strata, so the pair is a branching dichotomy, not a containment.
  VERDICT D: DISJOINT STRATA CONFIRMED

